This project ports designs and, in later stages, code from the following
open-source projects. Attribution is recorded here per the implementation
plan (section 12). Each entry says which parts are in the tree today and
which are not; the earlier "planned" marker outlived several of the things
it described, so entries now name the file instead.

huggingface/speech-to-speech (Apache-2.0)
  Realtime protocol conventions used as a reference spec; the generation
  invalidation semantics (design of pipeline/cancel_scope.py); the event
  injection pattern. normalize_realtime_url and its reconnect timeouts are
  NOT in the tree: our reconnect (src/bilisama/realtime/client.py) was
  written here. The upstream checkout is never vendored or modified: runtime
  patches live in tools/s2s_shim/ and are injected via PYTHONPATH.

QwenAudio/qwen-audio-agent (Apache-2.0)
  AnnouncementWindow, ported near line-for-line as the speaking-floor gate
  in src/bilisama/director/floor.py; batch-and-receipt delivery, split
  between ingest selection and the scheduler; the
  Provider/Protocol/Capabilities split in src/bilisama/realtime/; the serial
  command queue in src/bilisama/realtime/client.py (all landed 2026-08-11).
  The desktop-pet preview (landed 2026-08-14)
  ports its sprite-skin animation model (web/src/sprite-orb.js, itself
  aligned with OpenAI Codex's codex-rs/tui/src/pets track shapes) into
  src/bilisama/ui/web/js/skins/sprite.js, and follows its renderer-server
  token-prefix pattern and desktop-orb window recipe.

liliMozi/openhanako (Apache-2.0)
  Persona layering with its lazy fallback chain (src/bilisama/persona/
  loader.py) and the SQLite fact store (src/bilisama/memory/), both landed
  2026-08-11. The MoodParser incremental tag state machine is not in the
  tree: it belongs to the TTS chain, which is unwritten. The hanako, ming and
  butter persona texts under config/personas/ are ported verbatim from its
  identity/ishiki templates; their proactive prompts adapt its yuan scaffolds.

Project-N-E-K-O/N.E.K.O (Apache-2.0)
  Danmaku scoring order (guard > admin > medal > level > length,
  livedanmaku.py:477, renormalised to 0..1), the windowed pick-one
  selection, the paid-event lane, and the safety values our components
  reuse: 0.35s dedup window, 3-failures/60s breaker, and 1.0s combo settle
  with 600s suppression (landed 2026-08-13). The initially reused 60s
  per-uid cooldown was retired on 2026-08-28: same-viewer follow-ups now
  compete on content value alone.

Open-LLM-VTuber (MIT)
  sentence_divider (CJK chunking) and tts_manager ordered delivery: not in
  the tree, src/bilisama/tts/ is an empty package. The interruption memory
  rewrite is likewise unwritten — nothing truncates a remembered reply to
  what the audience actually heard.

xfgryujk/blivedm (MIT)
  Bilibili live protocol client, vendored unmodified at
  src/bilisama/ingest/bilibili/_vendor/blivedm/ with its LICENSE preserved.
  dev branch @ 0da0c10fc50ed0ccd3e68c65f6a503cf3ca4198b, vendored 2026-08-13;
  provenance and re-vendor steps in that directory's VENDOR.md.

Live2D Cubism Core (proprietary, "Redistributable Code")
  Not in the tree. When it arrives it goes in unmodified, with its copyright
  header intact and a separate LICENSE-Live2D.md. The commercial gate — what
  has to be true before anything ships publicly — is in
  docs/live2d-licensing.md.
